# SYNOPSIS

```usage
vkgen HEADER.h COMMANDS.swift vk.xml
vkgen --loader DISPATCH.swift vk.xml
vkgen --venus HEADER.h PROTOCOL.swift ENTRIES.swift \
  vk.xml SERIALIZATION.xml VENUS.xml
```

# DESCRIPTION

vkgen reads Khronos's Vulkan registry, `data/vulkan/vk.xml`, and writes the Vulkan API the graphics stack is built on: a C header of its types, laid out as C lays them out, and a Swift table of its commands.
Only the selection in `graphics/vulkan/gen/Selection.swift` is written: core 1.0 to 1.4 and the extensions Loinnir needs.

With `--loader`, it writes the Vulkan loader's dispatch tables and exported trampolines (`graphics/vulkan/loader/generated/Dispatch.swift`) from the same selection.

With `--venus`, it reads Venus's registries in `data/venus` (vk.xml with Venus's `VK_EXT_command_serialization.xml` as SERIALIZATION.xml and `VK_MESA_venus_protocol.xml` as VENUS.xml) and writes the Vulkan types as a C header (`TDVenus`), Venus's encoders and decoders (`Venus`), and the client driver's entry points it doesn't write by hand (`graphics/venus/driver/generated/Entries.swift`).

The outputs are committed. After changing the data, the selection or a generator, regenerate them; VenusTests fails when the committed outputs differ from what the data gives.

# EXAMPLES

```text
cd graphics/vulkan
../../.build/debug/vkgen c/include/td_vulkan.h \
  swift/generated/Commands.swift ../../data/vulkan/vk.xml
```

